{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Vanessa and Sally Plan a Party", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Gift of the Gab", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 9, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 16, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": " Describe routines and regular activities in a wider range of social and work contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to describe people's behavior and personality.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Talking About Future Actions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use four different tenses to talk about the future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"italic\">present simple</span> to talk about something scheduled or in a timetable. <br>For example: <br><span class=\"italic\">Our train <span class=\"strong\">leaves</span> at 9:00 a.m. on Monday morning.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"italic\">present continuous</span> for plans or arrangements.<br>For example: <br><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">I'm playing</span> football tomorrow with my friends.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">will</span> to make predictions about the future. Often we use words like: I think, maybe and I suppose, when we make these predictions.<br> For example: <br><span class=\"italic\">I think Italy <span class=\"strong\">will win</span> the World Cup.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You also use <span class=\"italic\">will</span> to make offers or promises, and when you decide at the moment of speaking. <br> For example: <br><span class=\"italic\">Mary <span class=\"strong\">will help</span> you with your homework.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">(be) going to</span> to talk about plans and intentions. You have the idea, but you have not booked or made a firm commitment yet.<br> For example: <br>I'<span class=\"strong\">m going to go</span> to a quiet, sunny place this summer on my vacation.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You also use <span class=\"italic\">(be) going to</span> when we can see something is likely to happen. There is some evidence that it is going to happen.<br> For example: <br><span class=\"italic\">Be careful! <span class=\"strong\">You are going to fall</span>.</span> <span class=\"prelo-letter-page-break\">", "type": "text"}, {"content": "To learn more, look at the chart below:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Going to</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Will</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Present Continuous</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Present Simple</span> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"decision made for the future\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"prediction about the future\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"action already arranged for the near future\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"timetables\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"conclusion with regard to the future\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"promise\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"fixed arrangements in the near future\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"spontaneous decision or offer\\\"}\",\"\",\"\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Respond Politely to Suggestions and Offers", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When someone offers suggestions, it is important to respond politely<br>Remember to use the modals <span class=\"italic\">could</span>, <span class=\"italic\">should</span> or <span class=\"italic\">might</span> to suggest something.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": " Here is a list of expressions you can use to give suggestions:<br>  <ul><li>You might want to \u2026</li> <li>Would you mind \u2026 ?</li> <li>You should \u2026</li> <li>You ought to \u2026 (strong request)</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Responding to Offers and Suggestions\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<ul><li>I don't think I can \u2026</li> <li>I guess that could ...</li> <li>That would be \u2026</li> <li>I would \u2026</li> <li>Don't mind if I do!</li></ul>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Ann</span>: Would you like more poutine?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Bob</span>: Don't mind if I do! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\"> Ann</span>: Would you mind if I do a profile on you? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Bob</span>: It would be a pleasure.", "type": "example"}]}, {"content": "engenn6le16ob09re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "heavenly", "type": "name"}, {"content": "delicious (about food) ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The food is heavenly!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le16ob09aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "gifted ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "extremely skilled", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Vanessa is an exceptionally gifted cook.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le16ob09aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "Don't mind if I do!", "type": "name"}, {"content": " I would really like that! ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Ann: Would you like more poutine? Bob: Don't mind if I do!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le16ob09aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "gig  ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "show, usually for music ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We're playing 8 gigs in total.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le16ob09aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "exhausting ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "tiring ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Playing gigs all the time sounds exhausting!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le16ob09aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "on the road ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "away from home; traveling ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I love life on the road!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le16ob09aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "reserved ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "shy", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm naturally quite reserved.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le16ob09aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "profile", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a long interview, usually about a famous person", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": " Example: Would you mind if I write a profile on you?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le16ob09aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"cont